{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The U-Net architecture is the gold standard for semantic image segmentation, consisting of a contracting path (encoder) to capture context and a symmetric expanding path (decoder) for precise spatial localization, linked via skip connections."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["Input Image ──► [ DoubleConv ] ────────────────────── Skip ─────────────────────► [ Up + Conv ] ──► Mask","                     │                                                                ▲","                  [ Down ] ──► [ DoubleConv ] ──────── Skip ───────► [ Up + Conv ] ───┘","                                   │                                     ▲","                                [ Down ] ──► [ Bottleneck Conv ] ────────┘"]},{"text":"1. Initializing and Running U-Net","anchor":"1-Initializing-and-Running-U-Net","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftVision","","\/\/ Initialize U-Net on Apple Silicon Metal GPU","let unet = UNetArchitecture(inChannels: 3, outChannels: 1, baseFeatures: 32)","","\/\/ Forward pass on image tensor (Batch x Height x Width x Channels)","let imageTensor = try ImageTensorLoader.load(url: URL(fileURLWithPath: \"sample.jpg\"))","let maskOutput = try unet.forward(image: imageTensor)","","print(\"Output mask dimensions: \\(maskOutput.shape)\")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Train and deploy deep convolutional U-Net neural networks for image segmentation directly on Apple Silicon MLX GPU.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftVision\/documentation\/SwiftVision"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftVision\/documentation\/SwiftVision\/UNetSegmentationArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/docume